participant "email_otps" as Table <<entity>>

Actor -> Page: 1: Enter email; request registration code
activate Page
Page -> API: 2: POST /api/auth/register/request-otp
activate API
API -> API: 3: Check rate limit and validate input
alt Valid request
API -> Service: 4: Request registration OTP
activate Service
Service -> Service: 5: Normalize email; check that no account already exists
Service -> Table: 6: Invalidate old OTPs; INSERT salted OTP hash and expiry
activate Table
Table --> Service: 7: OTP record saved
deactivate Table
Service -> Service: 8: Send registration OTP through email delivery adapter
Service --> API: 9: OTP delivery result and expiry
API --> Page: 10: HTTP 200: OTP delivery result and expiry
Page --> Actor: 11: Show authorized result
deactivate Service
else Invalid input or request unavailable
API --> Page: 4.1: HTTP 422 (429 only if rate-limited)
Page --> Actor: 4.2: Show appropriate error; retain form/draft
end
deactivate API
deactivate Page

legend left
Scope: Store OTP hashes only. Duplicate email returns 409; SMTP failure is not successful delivery.
endlegend
